Damien was the voice that spoke over the loudspeakers of [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/index|the lava ruin]], watching whoever entered through the ruin's cameras. He warned them off the heat and told them how the ruin's gates were worked, and he spoke of the suited workers as the workers, who cannot work the valves themselves. His accent was not [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oreskian]], and he said only that he came from north of the ruin. The name [[Geography/Althane/Athrea/Noxfell|Noxfell]] sounded familiar to him, though he did not think it was quite the name he knew.

He said he was human, claimed ten fingers, and believed he was trapped in the one room the cameras could not see, behind a locked door at the back of the gear chamber. That room was the ruin's control system. He was there: a single worker strapped into a leather chair, pipes running down from the ceiling into his suit, a walkie-talkie at his shoulder. He had been wired into the ruin's controls so long that he did not know his own body. When the Weft opened the door and pulled him free of the pipes, he died. With him gone the ruin ran itself, drained the lava from the passages and opened the bridge across it.
